# Copyable chat output

Cursor shows a copy control on fenced code blocks, not on ordinary prose.

When the reply contains anything Joel may need to copy — commands, emails, paths, HEAD SHAs, Alembic revisions, report field blocks, paste-back templates — put that content in a fenced code block.

Do this even when the same facts also appear in prose.

Do not leave copyable commands or report blocks in prose only.

Keep secrets, passwords, and SECRET_KEY values out of chat, fenced or not.
